cvcpkg: let lupa build lupa.lua54 / lupa.luajit21 against INSTALLED Lua libraries.

1. Upstream setup.py either compiles the Lua sources bundled under third-party/
   into each extension (modules lupa.lua54, lupa.luajit21, ...) or, with
   --no-bundle, links ONE pkg-config-discovered Lua into a single module named
   lupa.lua. Neither builds the per-version modules against an external Lua.
   This adds $LUPA_EXTERNAL_LUA: a JSON object mapping module name -> include
   dirs / library dirs / libraries, one extension per entry. Without the
   variable setup.py behaves exactly as upstream.

2. Drop setup(test_suite=...). setuptools removed the `test` command and that
   keyword in v72, so with a current setuptools it does nothing -- except when
   an older setuptools dist-info is still on the path (python311 bundles
   setuptools 65.5 next to the setuptools-cp311 column): its stale
   distutils.setup_keywords entry point then maps test_suite to
   setuptools.dist:check_test_suite, which no longer exists, and metadata
   generation fails with AttributeError (seen on the dev cluster's cp311 build).

